# function pick(c, v) { if (c === null) return one(v).x; if (c === undefined) return two(v).y; return v; }
# below each head of the framed part the call alone reads v, and no way leads from there to the reads of the later arms. So v is neither moved to a register that callees save nor stored, and no setup saves a register
# f1 = pick, f2 = one, f3 = two. pick is handed to sink
# REQUIRES: unsanitized-code
# RUN: allocate f1:Body mechanisms=none+DirectCalls
# CHECK-LABEL: unit f1:Body
# CHECK-NOT: usedCalleeSaves
# CHECK: headOfFramedPart =
# CHECK-NEXT: headOfFramedPart =
# CHECK-NOT: needsFrameAheadOfFramedPart
# PROGRAM-OF: two-parts-that-call-each-set-up-their-frame.ir
